A||||6||newfie||Thinkin of buying, never owned a fiero, need help||||5||
Z||000000||newfie||04-23-2000||10:20 PM||||I've never owned a fiero and don't know anything about them so I'm looking for some info.  Is there a site around that explains the basics of Fiero's.  For example what are the different models, What are the engines available, what does 2m4 mean? What type of performance can I get out of one? Is there a big aftermarket? I would appreciate any help. I don't want to end up giving in and buying a Camaro or Mustang( like everyone else)||||reg||5
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||04-23-2000||10:27 PM||||Well you've come to the right place for info. 2M4 is the designation for a 4 clyinder Fiero. 2M6 is the 6 clyinder version. And unless you are prepaired to totally fall in love with your car ...Don't buy a Fiero...lol. My 2M4 gets about 32 mpg and coners like it's on a rail. I LOVE IT !!!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Cooter||04-23-2000||10:48 PM||||Everything that I ever learned about a Fiero came from here! Hang out with us, learn about the cars and then start shopping. I wish that I had came here before I bought my 85 SE. If I had known then what I know now, I would have only one Fiero instead of two. After learning about the 88's, I had to have one so now I have a red 88 GT to match my red 85. Both are great cars, just great for different reasons. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||04-23-2000||10:51 PM||||OK newfie you want to know how big the after market is and were to find information on this mid engine car than try this <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Turbochargers" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html#Turbochargers</A>  I call this link ton's of fiero links. <P>Engines available are 2.5 liter 4 (92-96 HP) and 2.8 (140 HP). There are many upgrades for the v6 engine. Try here,  <A HREF="http://hometown.aol.com/gpxss/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://hometown.aol.com/gpxss/index.html</A>  <BR>and here, <A HREF="http://www.users.uswest.net/~racing2win/mild2wld.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.users.uswest.net/~racing2win/mild2wld.htm</A>  <BR>and here, <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A>  <BR>and here, <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A>  <BR>and here,  <A HREF="http://www.americancustomeng.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.americancustomeng.com/</A>   <BR>and here, <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm</A>  <BR>and here,<BR> <A HREF="http://www.users.uswest.net/~racing2win/mild2wld.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.users.uswest.net/~racing2win/mild2wld.htm</A>  <P>For places to get parts and performance parts go to these places. <A HREF="http://www.leaderind.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.leaderind.com/</A>   Called the Fiero Store, great place.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/</A>  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A>   <BR>I could do this all day but I think you have enough information here to keep you busy for days. <P>Good luck.<P><p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 04-23-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||sdm1964||04-24-2000||07:47 AM||||you fogot this: <A HREF="http://www.thefieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefieroproject.com</A> <BR>or this         <A HREF="http://www.fieroowners.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroowners.com</A> <BR>I would also see if you could find a fiero club in your area. Take a test drive in the different models. 88 formula, I thought it was manditory to own more than one fiero to be a member of this forum. And you will love them all.||||reg||7
Z||000005||88formula||04-24-2000||05:02 PM||||sdm1964, I used to own two (Formula and 87 coupe) but I like the formula a lot better than the coupe and owning two in my city is EXPENSIVE.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||85SE||04-26-2000||11:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sdm1964:<BR><B>I would also see if you could find a fiero club in your area. Take a test drive in the different models. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>newfie and I are in the same faculty at Memorial University in Newfoundland, Canada.  There's no Fiero club here.  Heck, there's hardly any Fieros here!  A few dozen around I guess.  You can count the 88s that I know of on one hand.  But we're trying!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>newfie - my offer stands.  Fell free to drop by and look at my car.  But it's probably going in the garage tomorrow to get some TLC done, so let me know.||||reg||10
